        <p>No 1595</p>
        <p>COCUNITY BOROUGH Oli` WARRINoum._ SHOP HOURS ACT, 1901.</p>
        <p>HAIRDRIPSERb' AND BAR.BRRS' SHOPS.</p>
        <p>WHEREAS the Town Council of the County Bornugk of Warrington are satisfied on representations made to them) that a prima facie case has been made out for making a Closing Order :—NOIIOII IS HERRBY GIVRN that it is the intentioß of the Council to ;ware an Order fixing the hours at which Hairdressers'and Harbert' shops shall be closed (on each day of the week) (in the said Boromgb) as set forth in the Draft Order annevd hereto.. Any person may make objections to the making of the Order or suggestions as to its provisions in a writts-n state- ment achires.ed to the Town Clerk before the expiration of four weeks from the Oess hereof. i.e. before the sth day of November 1907. On the expiration of the said period. the Council will take into consideration the objections or suggestions received and de,d(te as to proceeding further with the Order. NoTICII IS FURTHRR GIVEN that, during the said period, the occupier of any shop to be affected by the Order may, on presenting himself at the Office of the Inspector of the Nuisances at the Town Hall between the hours of Ten and Five on any day (except Saturday), verify that his name, address and trade are duly entered in the Register of bhops. Dated this sth day of October 1907. LYON WHITTLE, Town Clerk. Town Hall, Warrington.</p>
        <p>"A copy of the Draft Order referred t, in this notice may be obtained on appliceion by any ratepoiyer concerned at the Offices of the Town Clerk or lnepe2tor of nui.ances at the Town Hall.</p>
        <p>BIITABLIIIHED 1833.</p>
        <p>Mrs.</p>
        <p>i HOS.</p>
        <p>CLARhE,</p>
        <p>STATIONER AND NEWSAGENT, "EXAMINER " OFFICE. 33 MARKET STREET, EARLESTOWB. FANCY STATIONERY SUITABLE FOR PRESENTS.</p>
        <p>Mimi</p>
